SUMMARY:Beyond Academia Job Search Series: How to "Do" Networking
DESCRIPTION:You've probably heard networking is an important component of
  job/internship search. But what exactly is it\, and how do you do it? I
 n this workshop\, learn how to: - Use tools from Princeton (e.g.\, Caree
 r Compass\, TigerNet) to identify potential contacts - Create a list of 
 questions for informational interviews - Build and maintain relationship
 s over time This event is part of the Beyond Academia Job Search series.
  All sessions are 12-1 p.m. - CVs & Resumes - Wednesday\, Sept. 9 - Navi
 gating the Non-Academic Job Market - Thursday\, Sept. 24 - How to “Do
 ” Networking - Tuesday\, Oct. - Humanities and Social Science Research
  Careers Outside Academia - Tuesday\, Oct. 20 - STEM Research Careers Ou
 tside Academia - Thursday\, Oct. 22 This program is open to all Princeto
 n University graduate students regardless of identity. Email [careerdeve
 lopment@princeton.edu](mailto:careerdevelopment@princeton.edu\nRegister:
  https://princeton.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1978797\nhttps://careerd
 evelopment.princeton.edu/events/beyond-academia-job-search-series-how-do
 -networking
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/beyond-academia-job-se
 arch-series-how-do-networking
