SUMMARY:Arts at Work: Jim Lee '86 Comic Book Illustration Workshop & Lunc
 h
LOCATION:Hagan Studio
DESCRIPTION:World-renowned comic book artist\, writer\, editor\, publishe
 r and Chief Creative Officer of DC Comics Jim Lee '86 will demonstrate h
 is craft and guide participants through a series of illustration exercis
 es. Drawing materials will be provided for students who pre-register. St
 udents are invited to the workshop from 10:30-12 p.m.\, followed by a ne
 tworking lunch from 12-1 p.m. Open to Princeton students\; advanced regi
 stration required. Presented as part of the Arts At Work program by the 
 Center for Career Development and Lewis Center for the Arts. This progra
 m is part of the G. S. Beckwith Gilbert '63 Lecture Series. Arts at Work
  illustrates possible career paths in the arts and creative fields\, and
  forges connections between current students and alumni. This program is
  open to all Princeton University undergraduate and graduate students re
 gardless of identity. Email [careerdevelopment@prince\nAudience: Graduat
 e Students\, Undergraduate Students\nRegister: https://app.joinhandshake
 .com/edu/events/1992711\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/
