SUMMARY:The Brattle Group Presents: Introduction to Economic Modeling
LOCATION:Louis A. Simpson International Building A71
DESCRIPTION:Discover how economic\, financial and analytical models help 
 solve some of today's most complex business\, legal and public policy ch
 allenges. In this introductory session\, students will learn how economi
 c consultants use data\, theory and quantitative analysis to answer high
 -stakes questions involving competition\, regulation\, damages\, valuati
 on and strategy. Whether studying economics\, finance\, mathematics\, st
 atistics\, public policy or a related field\, students will gain insight
  into how analytical thinking translates into real-world decision-making
 . There will be information on internship and full-time opportunities at
  The Brattle Group. Brattle is a global economic consulting firm that he
 lps corporations\, law firms and governments address complex economic\, 
 financial and regulatory issues. The teams combine rigorous analysis wit
 h practical insight\, working alongside leading academics and \nhttps://
 careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/brattle-group-presents-introducti
 on-economic-modeling
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/brattle-group-presents
 -introduction-economic-modeling
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
