 rincetonians pursue. This event will feature a keynote from a special al
 umni guest\, panels\, breakout sessions and networking. Students will le
 arn about various careers in public service\, including: - Federal and l
 ocal government - AI and public service careers - Nonprofits - Think tan
 ks - Public-private partnerships - Public finance Alumni will discuss cu
 rrent trends\, pathways into public service and their own career journey
 s. A networking reception will follow. Co-sponsored by the School of Pub
 lic and International Affairs and the Center for Career Development. Thi
 s program is part of the G. S. Beckwith Gilbert '63 Lecture Series. This
  program is open to all Princeton University undergraduate and graduate 
 students regardless of identity. Email [careerdevelopment@princeton.edu]
 (mailto:careerdevelopment@princeton.edu) to request\nAudience: Graduate 
 Students\, Undergraduate Students\nRegister: https://app.joinhandshake.c
 om/edu/events/1977054\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/pu
 blic-service-career-day-2
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/public-service-career-
 day-2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
